{
  "_note": "Darkheart adversary affinity (PD-099): a small, explicit, reviewable classification of the catalogue adversaries the Darkheart pilot can use, into a handful of themes (PD-104 added `folk`: humanoid and socially interactive groups, the preferred neutral encounter). A scene's `encounter.themes` (data/darkheart-scenes.json) says which themes belong to it; an adversary no theme lists is never recommended on its own. Not a taxonomy of the whole bestiary and never read for anything else. `related` themes are allowed only as role fillers. scripts/validate-data.js checks every id against data/prep.json. PD-108: `neutral` is not a scene theme but the curated top-up — adversaries at home in any part of the forest, at least six per tier — that the engine adds, at the party's own tier only, when a scene's own candidates are fewer than six; it is never offered as a Master's theme.",
